#define ST_IS_MK2                   ST_MCU_ADDR+$0008 /* 1 on Mk.II. m3nu.bin is shared by every config, so anything the mk2 firmware cannot carry has to be gated at runtime: the patch-selector context menu OPENS there, but its "create patched ROM" entry is greyed (mfunc_isenabled_patch_export) and refused outright at the top of patch_create_rom, because the export handler is compiled out of the mk2 build for lack of flash. The menu's other entry (header mode) works on the mk2 -- CMD_PATCH_META_SAVE is built for every config. Lockstep with mcu_status_t.is_mk2 in src/snes.h (offset = field order; both were written against +$0007 in parallel branches). */

